<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Motion Study — {{ video_name }}</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --ink: #16191d; --muted: #5d666f; --line: #e2e6ea;
    --bg: #ffffff; --panel: #f7f9fb; --accent: #0072B2; --warn: #b45309;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink);
    font: 15px/1.55 -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  .wrap { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 28px 22px 70px; }
  header { border-bottom: 3px solid var(--ink); padding-bottom: 16px; margin-bottom: 26px; }
  h1 { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 25px; letter-spacing: -0.3px; }
  .sub { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
  h2 {
    font-size: 19px; margin: 40px 0 6px;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); padding-left: 10px;
  }
  .lede { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 14px; font-size: 14px; max-width: 78ch; }

  .cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(148px, 1fr)); gap: 12px; margin: 22px 0; }
  .card { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 9px; padding: 13px 15px; }
  .card .v { font-size: 25px; font-weight: 650; letter-spacing: -0.5px; }
  .card .k { font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.55px; margin-top: 3px; }

  table.data { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 13.5px; margin-top: 8px; }
  table.data th, table.data td { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 7px 10px; text-align: left; }
  table.data th { background: var(--panel); font-weight: 620; white-space: nowrap; }
  table.data tr:hover td { background: #fbfcfd; }
  .scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .empty { color: var(--muted); font-style: italic; }

  .tabs { display: flex; gap: 6px; margin: 10px 0 4px; }
  .tabs button {
    font: inherit; font-size: 13.5px; padding: 6px 14px; cursor: pointer;
    border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--panel); border-radius: 7px; color: var(--muted);
  }
  .tabs button.on { background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); color: #fff; font-weight: 600; }
  .pane { display: none; }
  .pane.on { display: block; }

  .note {
    background: #fff8e6; border: 1px solid #f0d9a0; border-left: 4px solid var(--warn);
    padding: 11px 14px; border-radius: 7px; margin: 14px 0; font-size: 13.5px;
  }
  pre.breakdown {
    background: #12161a; color: #dfe6ec; padding: 16px 18px; border-radius: 8px;
    overflow-x: auto; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.45;
    font-family: "Cascadia Mono", Consolas, "Courier New", monospace;
  }
  code { background: var(--panel); padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 92%; }
  .legend-key { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .legend-key b { color: var(--ink); }
  footer { margin-top: 52px; padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--muted); font-size: 12.5px; }
  @media print { .tabs { display: none; } .pane { display: block !important; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

<header>
  <h1>Motion &amp; Time Study — {{ video_name }}</h1>
  <div class="sub">
    Camera <b>{{ camera_id }}</b>{% if description %} · {{ description }}{% endif %}
    · Recording length {{ duration_hms }} · Generated {{ generated_at }}
  </div>
</header>

{% if warnings %}
  {% for w in warnings %}<div class="note">{{ w }}</div>{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

<div class="cards">
  <div class="card"><div class="v">{{ headline.workers }}</div><div class="k">Workers</div></div>
  <div class="card"><div class="v">{{ "%.0f"|format(headline.mean_utilisation) }}%</div><div class="k">Mean utilisation</div></div>
  <div class="card"><div class="v">{{ headline.distinct_steps }}</div><div class="k">Work elements</div></div>
  <div class="card"><div class="v">{{ headline.total_stops }}</div><div class="k">Stops detected</div></div>
  <div class="card"><div class="v">{{ "%.0f"|format(headline.total_stop_s) }}s</div><div class="k">Total idle at station</div></div>
  <div class="card"><div class="v">{{ "%.0f"|format(headline.total_walking_s) }}s</div><div class="k">Total walking</div></div>
</div>

<h2>Operation timeline</h2>
<p class="lede">
  Each row is one worker across the real clock of the operation. Bar colour identifies
  the employee; texture identifies the activity — solid is working at a station,
  hatched is walking, faded is away.
</p>
<div class="legend-key">
  <b>■ amber square</b> = stopped (present at the station but not moving for
  {{ stop_min_seconds }}s or more) &nbsp;·&nbsp;
  <b>✖ red cross</b> = left (out of view). Hover any bar or marker for exact times.
</div>
<div class="tabs">
  <button class="on" onclick="tab(this,'g1')">Colour by employee</button>
  <button onclick="tab(this,'g2')">Colour by work element</button>
</div>
<div id="g1" class="pane on">{{ gantt_worker|safe }}</div>
<div id="g2" class="pane">{{ gantt_step|safe }}</div>

<h2>Work element times</h2>
<p class="lede">
  Read the <b>cv_percent</b> column first. It is the spread as a percentage of the
  average, so it flags the <em>inconsistent</em> steps — which is usually where
  recoverable time is hiding, more so than the merely slow ones.
  <br><b>normal_s</b> = mean × rating factor {{ rating_factor }}.
  <b>standard_s</b> = normal + {{ "%.0f"|format(allowance_percent) }}% allowances.
</p>
<div class="scroll">{{ table_steps|safe }}</div>

<h2>Where each worker's time went</h2>
<p class="lede">
  Utilisation is time at a work station as a share of time on camera — not of the whole
  recording, so a worker who appears late is not penalised for it.
</p>
<div class="scroll">{{ table_workers|safe }}</div>

<h2>Cycle times</h2>
<div class="scroll">{{ table_cycles|safe }}</div>

<h2>Standard Work Combination Table</h2>
<p class="lede">
  One chart per operator, showing a single repeatable cycle broken into its elements
  and averaged across every cycle observed.
  <b style="color:#0072B2">━━ Manual</b> is the operator's hands on the work.
  <b style="color:#E69F00">- - Auto / wait</b> is the operator present at the station but
  not moving.
  <b style="color:#009E73">∿∿ Walk</b> is transport, charged to the element it follows.
  {% if takt_seconds %}The heavy red line is <b>takt</b> — demand rate. Anything to the
  right of it is a cycle that cannot keep up.{% endif %}
</p>
<div class="note">
  <b>What "auto / wait" does and does not mean.</b> A classic Standard Work Combination
  Table separates <em>machine</em> time (the press is cycling, the operator is genuinely
  free) from <em>waiting</em> (avoidable). Video cannot tell those apart — both look like a
  person standing still at a station. This chart reports the honest measurement,
  "operator not moving at the station", and leaves the split to whoever knows the
  equipment cycle times. Do not present that column as machine time without checking.
</div>

{% for block in swct_blocks %}
  <h3 style="margin:26px 0 2px;font-size:16px;">
    {{ block.worker }}
    <span style="font-weight:400;color:#5d666f;font-size:13.5px;">
      — cycle {{ "%.1f"|format(block.cycle_s) }}s, averaged over {{ block.observations }}
      observed cycle{{ "s" if block.observations != 1 }}
    </span>
  </h3>
  {{ block.html|safe }}
{% else %}
  <p class="empty">No standard work data. Set <code>cycles.boundary_zone</code> in the config.</p>
{% endfor %}

<h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-top:26px;">Totals per operator</h3>
<div class="scroll">{{ table_swct_totals|safe }}</div>

<h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-top:22px;">Element detail</h3>
<div class="scroll">{{ table_swct|safe }}</div>

<h2>Labour balance (Yamazumi)</h2>
<p class="lede">
  Work content per operator, per cycle. Uneven columns mean the line is unbalanced:
  the tallest column sets the pace and every shorter one is waiting.
</p>
{{ yamazumi|safe }}

<h2>Movement paths (spaghetti diagram)</h2>
<p class="lede">Every worker's floor path over the whole recording. Dense tangles are walking that the layout is forcing.</p>
{{ spaghetti|safe }}

<h2>Event log</h2>
<p class="lede">Every stop and departure, in order.</p>
<div class="scroll">{{ table_events|safe }}</div>

<h2>Full step breakdown (text)</h2>
<p class="lede">
  Every step each worker performed, in order, with its start time and duration —
  the same content as <code>steps.txt</code> in this run folder. This is the listing to
  check against what you saw on the floor.
</p>
<details>
  <summary style="cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;padding:8px 0;">Show the full listing</summary>
  <pre class="breakdown">{{ breakdown_text }}</pre>
</details>

<footer>
  Analysed at {{ analysis_fps }} fps (pose {{ pose_fps }} fps).
  A worker counts as stopped below {{ stop_threshold }} body-heights/second of hand
  movement for {{ stop_min_seconds }}s or more.
  <br>
  The <b>rating factor of {{ rating_factor }}</b> was entered by a human observer — this
  system does not estimate worker pace, and no standard time here is valid without a
  qualified observer standing behind that number.
</footer>

</div>
<script>
function tab(btn, id) {
  var tabs = btn.parentNode.querySelectorAll('button');
  for (var i = 0; i < tabs.length; i++) tabs[i].classList.remove('on');
  btn.classList.add('on');
  var panes = document.querySelectorAll('.pane');
  for (var j = 0; j < panes.length; j++) panes[j].classList.remove('on');
  var el = document.getElementById(id);
  el.classList.add('on');
  // Plotly sizes to a hidden container as zero-width; nudge it once shown.
  if (window.Plotly) {
    var plots = el.querySelectorAll('.js-plotly-plot');
    for (var k = 0; k < plots.length; k++) window.Plotly.Plots.resize(plots[k]);
  }
}
</script>
</body>
</html>
